.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt DTFL_STREAM_PARTITION 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_stream_partition
.Nd route a stream's records into several streams
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/timely_ops.h
.Ft void
.Fo dtfl_stream_partition
.Fa "dtfl_stream *st"
.Fa "size_t parts"
.Fa "size_t (*route)(void *ctx, const void *rec, size_t len)"
.Fa "dtfl_ctx ctx"
.Fa "dtfl_stream **outs"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn dtfl_stream_partition
produces
.Fa parts
output streams from
.Fa st .
For each record,
.Fa route
returns a part index less than
.Fa parts ,
and the record is sent to that part's stream at its original time.
A record whose index is not less than
.Fa parts
is dropped.
Each output carries the input's record type.
The streams are stored in
.Fa outs ,
which must have room for
.Fa parts
pointers.
.Pp
The context in
.Fa ctx
is passed to
.Fa route .
When
.Fa ctx
carries a destructor, the operator owns the context and releases it
when the operator is dropped.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn dtfl_stream_partition
returns no value; it stores
.Fa parts
output streams, owned by the scope, through
.Fa outs .
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
static size_t by_mod3(void *ctx, const void *rec, size_t len) {
	return (size_t)(dtfl_get_u64(rec) % 3);
}

dtfl_stream *outs[3];
dtfl_stream_partition(in, 3, by_mod3, DTFL_NOCTX, outs);
.Ed
.Sh ERRORS
.Fn dtfl_stream_partition
does not return an error code.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_stream_concat 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_stream_count 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_stream_exchange 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_stream_map 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_stream_ok_err 3 ,
.Xr dtfl 7
.Sh HISTORY
This is the C form of timely's
.Fn partition
operator.
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
The operator and its streams belong to the worker thread that built
them and must not be shared.
